# Runtime dependencies of the hosted image (Dockerfile). Only what the serving code imports: Django and its password
# hasher, the WSGI server, numpy/pandas (score store, untapped) and shapely (area geometry, imported lazily).
# geopandas, pyogrio, pyproj and requests build the stores on the laptop and are deliberately not in the image.
#
# The hashed lock (requirements.linux.lock, committed next to this file) is for CPython 3.12 on linux x86_64, wheels only. Regenerate
# it from any OS with pip alone (its header has the exact command): resolve with `pip install --dry-run --report` for
# --platform manylinux2014_x86_64 and manylinux_2_28_x86_64 (constrained with -c requirements.lock.txt, so the image runs the very
# versions CI tests), then list every PyPI wheel of each resolved version those tags accept with its sha256. The Dockerfile installs it with --require-hashes --no-deps, so every wheel is pinned by sha256.
Django>=5.2,<5.3
